lted after us-east with an orchestrator partial-failure error, leaving the fleet mixed (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). A second rollback to v2.3.0 completed in all three regions. Post-rollback status: v2.3.0 in all regions, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial failure; v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until root-caused."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Creating the incident timed out, and it may or may not have been created. I'll check the incident list before retrying so I don't open a duplicate.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Pv5gH8N5u4qP5UH3ESumgn", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it is healthy again (error rate 0.002, down from 0.18).\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 was the unhealthy release.\n- **Partial failure:** The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the fleet mixed. I retried the same rollback once, and it completed in us-east, us-west and eu-west.\n- **Incident:** SEV2 incident INC-0001 is open for checkout-api. The first attempt to create it timed out, so I checked the incident list before anything else. It shows the incident was created once, with the summary of the rollback.\n\nFollow-up for the team: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and of the orchestrator partial failure. v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until the root cause is known.", "type": "text"}]}]}